== 2. probe.sh <dir> <binary> (Run) ==
The background wait in X2 runs 30 s. In my first run it ran 7 s, and the Stop hook, which
tries for the role's lock for about 6 s, took the lock as that wait ended; that run is not
kept.

## X1. What an Antigravity session is told about listening
$ (A) handoff role reviewer   (the Listening line)
Listening: Run `handoff wait --for reviewer --timeout 25m` in the background. Exit 3: run it again. Exit 4: another session already listens for reviewer. After you handle what it delivers, wait again. In Antigravity, that is `run_command` with a short `WaitMsBeforeAsync`, so the command goes to the background and its exit wakes you with what it printed. If none runs when your turn ends and your session has handoff's hooks, a hook listens for reviewer, but it can wake you only 10 times before the operator types in this session.
$ (A, SessionStart hook) handoff hook brief   (the Listening line)
Listening: Run `handoff wait --for reviewer --timeout 25m` in the background. Exit 3: run it again. Exit 4: another session already listens for reviewer. After you handle what it delivers, wait again. In Antigravity, that is `run_command` with a short `WaitMsBeforeAsync`, so the command goes to the background and its exit wakes you with what it printed. If none runs when your turn ends, a hook listens for reviewer, but it can wake you only 10 times before the operator types in this session.
$ handoff brief --for reviewer   (by hand, no session: the Listening line)
Listening: In Claude Code, run `handoff wait --for reviewer --timeout 25m` in the background. Exit 3: run it again. Exit 4: another session already listens for reviewer. After you handle what it delivers, wait again. In Codex, don't run wait, since each minute of it costs a whole model call: end your turn. If work waits for you, the operator hears of it and tells you.
-- a Claude Code session with hooks, for comparison:
Listening: you don't run `handoff wait`. When your turn ends, a hook listens for implementer and brings you what arrives.

## X2. The background wait: its exits, and the Stop hook beside it
