## X3. The agent forgot to wait: the hook's wake, and its cap, as before
$ (Antigravity A, Stop hook, executionNum 3, fullyIdle true) handoff hook listen --timeout 1s
    continue | handoff: nothing new for reviewer in 1s. Just end your turn; listening starts again when it ends. Before your turn ends, run `handoff wait --for reviewer --timeout 25m` in the background, as your brief says, so this hook needn't wake you. / 
$ (Antigravity A, Stop hook, executionNum 10, fullyIdle true) handoff hook listen --timeout 1s
    (no wake) | 
  binding A: block: cap | listened: yes
  alerts to the operator: 1
    x1: handoff can't wake reviewer's Antigravity session for new work until you type in it: Antigravity lets hooks continue a turn 10 times in a row.
-- the agent runs the wait again: the block is over
  binding A: block: none | listened: yes

== 3. Source: how long the Stop hook tries for the lock ==
a.listen (cmd/handoff/session.go:471) tries wait.Listen 13 times, 250 ms apart, and each
wait.Listen tries 6 times, 50 ms apart (internal/wait/presence.go:61): about 6 s in all,
where the comment above a.listen says three. This is from before H34.

